    <h1>Scaling Prototyping Capability with AI-Led Design Tooling</h1>
    <p class="project-subtitle" style="text-align: center; color: var(--color-muted); margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      Giving Leadership Working, Code-Backed Prototypes to Review Asynchronously • Multi-Brand Systems Architecture
    </p>

    <!-- Executive Scorecard -->
    <div class="project-meta-list">
      <p><span class="meta-label">Leadership Role:</span> Lead Design Technologist &amp; AI Strategy Lead</p>
      <p><span class="meta-label">Scope &amp; Brand Footprint:</span> Multi-Brand Enterprise Ecosystem (Retail Front Store App &amp; Health100 Rx App)</p>
      <p><span class="meta-label">Cross-Functional Partners:</span> VP of Product Design, Digital Engineering Directors, Growth &amp; Rx Product Leads</p>
      <p><span class="meta-label">Core Business &amp; Ops Impact:</span> Replaced slow synchronous walkthroughs with <strong>always-on showcase hubs</strong>; compressed prototype build cycles from <strong>quarters to days</strong>; established <strong>automated heuristic scoring QA</strong> and in-context review pipelines.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="project-intro">
      Leadership review of complex design work traditionally relied on static mockups and scheduled calendar walkthroughs. That process was slow, synchronous, and detached from how the product actually feels in a user's hand. I led a small, AI-augmented design technology team to eliminate this bottleneck: we built a repeatable prototyping engine where designers translate design intent into interactive, on-brand prototypes, publish them to always-on showcase hubs, and collect contextual feedback asynchronously without booking a meeting.
    </p>

    <!-- Hubs Comparison Hero Grid -->
    <div class="image-grid-2">
