    <h2>3. Approach &amp; Technical Architecture</h2>

    <h3>A. Prototypes That Behave Like Shipped Software</h3>
    <p>
      Our core standard was simple: designers describe intent, and the engine produces an interactive, token-accurate prototype. Rather than a static clickable picture, stakeholders receive responsive software that navigates, transitions, and handles state changes identically to native code. That interactive fidelity is what makes asynchronous review effective; stakeholders cannot evaluate subtle micro-interactions or cognitive load from flat wireframes.
    </p>

