    <h2>4. Automated Trust: Quality Gates &amp; Heuristic Audits</h2>
    <p>
      Because prototypes went directly to executive leadership, platform reliability was paramount. We embedded automated validation gates into the publishing pipeline (including structural linting, token compliance, and visual regression checks) so that every published link worked reliably without manual QA bottlenecks.
    </p>
    <p>
      To elevate design craft at scale, we engineered an automated <strong>Heuristics Evaluation Engine</strong>. The system evaluates concepts against an established usability rubric and generates a leadership-ready scorecard complete with rationale and evidence across every category.
    </p>

    <!-- Heuristics Evaluation Report -->
    <img src="/images/ai-prototyping/heuristics-evaluation-report.png" alt="Automated Heuristics Evaluation Report comparing multiple design variations" class="project-image" loading="lazy" />
    <p class="image-caption">Automated Heuristic Audit: Three concepts for the same flow evaluated objectively against standardized usability criteria.</p>

    <h2>5. Closing the Asynchronous Feedback Loop</h2>
    <p>
      Solving the review bottleneck required redesigning both the artifact and the review workflow:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Structured Decision Hand-off Packets:</strong> Before opening a prototype, leadership reviews a succinct briefing card establishing specific decision points, out-of-scope boundaries, and underlying trade-offs to keep discussions focused on strategic priorities.</li>
      <li><strong>In-Context Screen Annotations:</strong> Reviewers drop pin-point comments directly onto specific prototype screens. Feedback routes automatically into active Slack channels and Jira trackers without forcing executives to learn a separate tool.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="image-grid-2">
