    </div>

    <h2>Quantified Business &amp; Operational Impact</h2>
    <div class="project-meta-list" style="margin: 2rem 0;">
      <p><span class="meta-label">Delivery Velocity:</span> Reduced high-fidelity prototype build times from <strong>3-4 weeks to under 48 hours</strong>.</p>
      <p><span class="meta-label">Executive Engagement:</span> 100% of executive prototype reviews transitioned to asynchronous, self-guided exploration across two dedicated showcase hubs.</p>
      <p><span class="meta-label">System Generalization:</span> Successfully scaled from Retail Front Store to Health100 without rebuilding foundational infrastructure, proving a repeatable enterprise capability.</p>
      <p><span class="meta-label">Evaluation Rigor:</span> Standardized automated heuristic scoring across 100% of concept variations prior to executive presentation.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Leadership Retrospective</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Fidelity is the Catalyst for Asynchronous Alignment:</strong> You cannot ask executives to evaluate complex products asynchronously using static mocks; they lack the tactile reality needed for confident decision-making. High-fidelity, code-backed prototypes eliminate the need for an explanatory meeting.</li>
      <li><strong>Architectural Judgment Separates AI Hype from Enterprise Reality:</strong> AI can rapidly generate components, but it cannot make strategic system-boundary decisions. Knowing when to decouple Health100 from Retail Front Store was an essential human judgment that protected both brand integrity and velocity.</li>
      <li><strong>Frictionless Feedback Belongs in Existing Ecosystems:</strong> Forcing stakeholders into new review portals guarantees drop-off. Capturing comments directly on the prototype and broadcasting them to existing Slack and project channels kept review velocity high.</li>
    </ol>
